Whilst on the subject of acquiring dragon armour, something strange
happened to me for which I would welcome some hints. I was playing a
priest who was reasonably equipped to take on a dragon, having boots
of speed and Excalibur, so I could hit it and step away without being
hit. I also had a wand of polymorph to apply to the corpse. So not
much later I had a nice suit of uncursed +0 Black Dragon Scale Mail.
Great I thought, this will do nicely until I can find the one I really
want, viz the Gray (spelling!) Dragon. Some time later however,
without as far as I know stepping on any form of trap I suddenly
polymorphed into a black dragon, getting a message like "You merge
with the scaly armour you're wearing" or some such. I searched around
to see if it was a polymorph trap but as far as I can tell it wasn't.
So my questions are:-
1) Why has this happened?
2) Could I have prevented it?
3) How can I polymorph back ( I can't wear any of my nice armour as a
dragon)
4) Is there any difference between created dragon scale mail and
wished for dragon scale mail.

Just for general interest, here are some observations from playing
this character. I like Priests cos I don't have to worry about things
being cursed. However, I found them quite hard to start. It didn't
seem to matter what I did, by the time I reached about level 6 (me,
not the dungeon), I would meet something I could in no way deal with,
and that would be that. My impression is that one is best off
exploring as much as possible looking for equipment, and letting one's
pet do the fighting, as the nature of the opponents seems more related
to one's character level than dungeon level. Anyway, the break for
this one came when he found a cursed scroll of genocide. I chose
nurses, and managed to increase my hit points from around 40 to around
100. The other break was finding boots of speed, these really are
amazingly useful for low level weedy characters. I have now also
acquired a cloak of displacement, helm of brilliance, Stormbringer and
several useful intrinsics and various other junk, so I was unhappy to
be turned into a dragon and be unable to use it. Ah well, all part of
nethack's rich tapestry I suppose!
